/ One column, three parts, and a hairline between them: the plea, the offer,
/ the decision. Nothing is boxed and nothing is stacked side by side, so the
/ page reads top to bottom in the same order on every screen.
/
/ The surface is flat and warm. A gradient and a panel on top of it were two
/ layers that carried no meaning of their own.
.relative.bg-amber-50.w-full
  / The page has three ways out, and each one gets a form of its own so they
  / are not read as one row of links: the corner dismisses the page, the button
  / below leads on, and the sentence in the plea links out.
  /
  / The corner of the surface is where a notice is closed, so the link sits
  / there and not in the column. Only an admin gets it: the skip is recorded
  / for them alone, and without that record the gate sends everyone else
  / straight back to this page.
  - if admin?
    = link_to registration_path(status: 'skip'),
              class: 'absolute right-4 top-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded text-sm text-gray-500 hover:text-gray-900 focus:outline-hidden focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo-500 focus:ring-offset-2 sm:right-6 sm:top-6 sm:text-base lg:right-8 click-animation',
              data: { turbo: false } do
      = t('sponsoring.show.skip')
      i.fas.fa-xmark.text-lg

  / A phone has no room beside the corner link, so there the content starts
  / below it.
  .max-w-5xl.mx-auto.px-4.sm:px-6.lg:px-8.pt-12.sm:pt-10.md:pt-14.pb-8.md:pb-14.text-base.md:text-lg
    / On a phone the headline needs the step to text-2xl: at text-xl it sits too
    / close to the plea below it, and the mark around it has nothing to hold.
    h1.text-2xl.md:text-4xl.font-bold.leading-relaxed
      span.bg-amber-300.box-decoration-clone.px-2.dark:text-gray-900
        == t('sponsoring.show.headline')

    / One rhythm for the whole page: every part keeps the same distance to the
    / hairline that separates it from the next one. A phone gets the smaller of
    / the two distances, so the whole page can stay on one screen there.
    .mt-6.md:mt-8.divide-y.divide-amber-200
      .pb-6.md:pb-8
        / max-w-prose keeps the line under 65 characters. Without it the
        / paragraph runs the full width of the page on a wide screen.
        p.max-w-prose.md:text-xl
          == t('sponsoring.show.p1')

      .py-6.md:py-8
        = render SponsoringBenefits::Component.new

        / A footnote to the list, not one more argument: it stays small and
        / quiet, and it keeps the short distance that binds it to the list. It
        / answers what the list raises, which is what the reader without a
        / subscription asks at that moment.
        p.mt-3.md:mt-4.max-w-prose.text-sm.text-gray-500.dark:text-gray-300
          = t('sponsoring.show.p4')

        / The link follows the list, because that is what it continues: it
        / leads to the page that describes every one of these features.
        /
        / It stays one step below the list. The list is the offer, the link only
        / points at more of it, so it must not be the larger of the two.
        .mt-5.md:mt-6
          = render Button::Component.new path: SolectrusLink.url('https://solectrus.de/sponsoring', campaign: 'sponsoring-page'),
                                         title: t('sponsoring.show.more'),
                                         type: :link,
                                         style: :secondary,
                                         options: { \
                                          class: 'text-base',
                                          rel: 'noopener',
                                          target: '_blank',
                                        }

      .pt-6.md:pt-8
        / Whoever is not an admin cannot start anything from here, so this
        / branch asks for the login first. What follows is the same row in both
        / cases, which is why the month is rendered once.
        - unless admin?
          p.max-w-prose
            = t('sponsoring.show.login_required')

        / The button and the month it can start share one line, the month at
        / the far end of it. A phone puts the month on the next line.
        .flex.flex-wrap.items-center.justify-between.gap-4 class=('mt-5' unless admin?)
          - if admin?
            = render Button::Component.new path: registration_path,
                                           title: t('sponsoring.show.continue'),
                                           type: :link,
                                           options: { \
                                            class: 'font-medium text-lg px-5',
                                            data: { turbo: false },
                                          }
          - else
            = render Button::Component.new path: new_session_path,
                                           title: t('layout.login')

          = render 'trial'
